Session restarts now tell three cases apart: real context exhaustion, a flatlining loop, and simply running out of iterations. The goal isn't done yet: the build loop doesn't call the new classifier anywhere, so nothing outside the tests detects a flatline yet.

**What changed** (committed as `04ca9ab2`):
- **`restart_detect_reason`** in `scripts/lib/session-restart.sh`:
  - It used to return `context_exhaustion` whenever the loop reached its iteration limit, which meant the `iteration_limit` branch could never run.
  - It now returns `context_exhaustion` only when the classifier actually found context-full evidence.
  - It returns `flatline` when enough iterations in a row (the threshold, 3 by default) changed no code and failed the same way.
  - Otherwise, reaching the limit returns `iteration_limit`.
  - The order of checks is: manual, context exhaustion, flatline, iteration limit, stuck loop.
- **`restart_suggest_strategy`** has a new critical-priority `flatline` strategy telling the fresh session to stop repeating its last attempt and try a different approach.
- **Tests** in `scripts/sw-session-restart-test.sh`: the old context-exhaustion test checked for the bug (reaching 10 of 10 iterations had to return `context_exhaustion`), so I changed it to require real evidence. I added tests for the iteration limit, flatline (including below-threshold and which-check-wins cases) and the flatline strategy.

**Test results:** the full `npm test` run passed all 163 suites. The `sw-cost-test.sh:226` error from last iteration didn't come back when I re-ran that suite, and that file isn't touched by this work, so I didn't change anything there. The audit finding was a failure in the audit tool itself (it rejected its own JSON schema), so it didn't point to any problem in the code.

**Done so far:** tasks 1, 5, 6 and 11.

**Next:** task 2, calling `flatline_classify_iteration` from `sw-loop.sh` on every iteration and emitting the classification and flatline events. Most of the remaining tasks wait on that.
